course: dictionary
lesson: 14391
title: Swinging back and forth: oscillation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oscillation is a regular movement back and forth. A swing is an everyday example: it goes forward, then back, then forward again. «The pendulum made one oscillation as it swung from the left to the right and back again.» Each complete trip counts as one oscillation.
explain: Scientists count oscillations to measure time. A pendulum always takes the same time for one full oscillation, so counting swings tells us how much time has passed. This time is called the period. «The pendulum made 10 oscillations in 20 seconds.» Share 20 seconds by 10 oscillations, and each oscillation takes 2 seconds.
explain: The word can also describe changes between two states, feelings or opinions. «Her mood had many oscillations between happy and sad.» Here the mood keeps going back and forth, like a pendulum. Check the clues: back and forth, between two things, is the key.
fact: An oscillation is a regular movement back and forth.
fact: One full oscillation means going from one side to the other and back again.
fact: The time for one full oscillation is called the period.
fact: Sound and light are oscillations: they are vibrations and waves.
fact: To find the time for one oscillation, divide the total time by the number of oscillations: 60 ÷ 30 = 2 seconds.
exercise: «The pendulum made 10 oscillations in 20 seconds.» How long does one oscillation take? | *2 seconds | 1 second | 20 minutes | 10 seconds
exercise: What is one full oscillation? | *One swing from one side to the other and back | A pause at the top of a swing | A single step forward | The end of a long journey
exercise: «Her mood had many oscillations between happy and sad.» What does oscillations mean here? | Long, slow walks | *Back-and-forth changes | Loud noises | Sudden stops
test: «A pendulum made 30 oscillations in 60 seconds.» How long does one oscillation take? | 30 seconds | *2 seconds | 60 seconds | 1 second
test: Which of these is an oscillation? | A car driving in a straight line to school | A closed door staying still | *A pendulum swinging left and right | A ball rolling down a hill once
exam: «A pendulum made 45 oscillations in 90 seconds.» How long does one full oscillation take, and what is the period? | 90 seconds | 45 seconds | 1 second | *2 seconds
